  "hints": [
    "Each position only cares about the tallest wall on its left and on its right.",
    "Precomputing left-max and right-max arrays works in O(n) space. Two pointers can do it in O(1).",
    "Keep lo, hi, left_max, right_max. Move the side with the lower wall: if heights[lo] < heights[hi], update left_max and add left_max - heights[lo], then lo += 1; otherwise mirror on the right."
  ],
  "followUps": [
    "Why is it safe to settle the lower side first when using two pointers?"
